WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.003
-The U.S. coronavirus outbreak
reached a grim new milestone

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.940
yesterday with over 3,000 deaths
in one day, a global record,

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.543
but the President was too busy
live-tweeting Fox News

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.978
and trying to get the results
of an election

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.279
he lost, overturned.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.616
For more on this, it's time
for A Closer Look.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:22.188
Every day it gets harder
and harder to articulate

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.590
just how shocking
and devastating and unbearable

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.061
this situation is and how sick
and depraved and sadistic

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.162
our leaders are.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.830
At some point, you just
run out of words.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.499
If, when this whole thing
started, you'd invested in

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:36.102
Purell, Lysol,
and thesaurus.com,

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.703
you would've made a fortune.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:41.073
A king's ransom,
a tidy nest egg, racks on racks.

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:44.143
Sadly, I put all my stock
in rhymezone.com

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.612
and it turns out even during
quarantine no one wants

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.982
my one-man Hanukkah-themed
parody of "Jersey Boys,"

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.450 line:0%
Jersey Goys.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.051 line:0%
♪ Menorah lights ♪

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:55.555
♪ We got a dreidel
instead of a tree ♪

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:58.157
♪ Ain't no prize
instead they're all for me ♪

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:01.260
♪ Oh, I love menorah lights ♪

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.562
In my friend group,
I've always been the Miranda,

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:06.532
but I guess I'm not
Lin-Manuel Miranda.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.268
Hey, guys.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:11.870
Camera operators, don't just
slip jokes in, okay?

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.440
I mean, I appreciate it,
but don't.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.176
Anyway, the point is,

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:17.776
we're in the midst
of a national calamity,

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:19.946
unlike anything most of us has
seen in our lifetimes.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:23.483
It's an ongoing emergency with
over 200,000 new cases every day

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.185
and 100,000 Americans in
the hospital as we speak.

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:30.323
Republicans spent over
$7 million in 2 1/2 years,

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.860
investigating four American
deaths in Benghazi in order to,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.963
by own admission, drag down
Hillary Clinton's poll numbers.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.765
But when you bring up COVID,

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.266
they act like it's a new
TikTok trend

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.400
they have never heard of before.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.835
Is that the one where you eat

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.771
cereal out
of someone else's mouth?

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.974
And as grotesque and sociopathic
is the indifference

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.175
and incompetence from
the Trump administration

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:51.577
and Republican party have been,

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:53.813
there's also plenty of blame
to go around

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.215
from confusing decisions
by local officials

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:59.452
to close playgrounds
but keep gyms and bars open,

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.520
to hypocrites like the mayor of
Austin who told

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.588
people to stay home

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.690
while he was on vacation
in Cabo.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.758
I mean, I'm sure it's
a wonderful place,

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.493
but just being in Cabo

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:08.728
sounds like
an admission of guilt.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.230
If somebody started
a sentence,

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.633
let me explain, I was in Cabo,
you would just say shut up.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:16.335
Unless of course you were
in Cancun in which case,

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:17.970
you know,
you'd have to hear them out.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.472
The response to the coronavirus

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.741
has been a total failure of
American governance

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.010
from the top down and leadership
is desperately needed.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.079
The President and his aides
could be on TV every day asking

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.449
people to stay home
for their own sake

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.917
and for the health of
their friends,

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.318
family, and fellow Americans,

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.685
they could be leading
the charge

00:02:33.685 --> 00:02:36.288
to get direct payments to
Americans and small businesses

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.258
to help them through
the crisis, instead,

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.893
Mitch McConnell has been
holding up an aid package

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.662
in order to get a liability
shield for corporations

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:45.531
that put workers in harm's way,

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:47.399
while the White House proposed

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.468
lowering the Federal
unemployment benefit

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:53.005
a situation that has clearly
infuriated Vermont Senator,

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.072
Bernie Sanders.

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:55.808
-Unemployment, a high.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.377
We have a record level of hunger
in America.

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:00.879
Millions of people
are facing evictions.

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:02.749
This is an emergency.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.350
Congress has to respond
aggressively

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.186
to help working families.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.155
You know, Stephanie,
I always get a kick.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.989
Here in Washington where
we go to war,

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:12.625
there's endless
amounts of money,

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.461
tax breaks for billionaires,
endless amounts of money.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.130
Corporate welfare,
endless amounts of money.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.033
When children are going hungry
in America today,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.868
suddenly,
we don't have enough money.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.504
That's crap, that's wrong.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.539
-Can Bernie be
the new host of "Jeopardy"?

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.240
That would be fantastic.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.608
-What is Los Angeles?

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:32.011
That's crap. That's wrong.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.713
Bernie's right, and there's
no better way to say it.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.050
The situation should be just as
outrageous to you as seeing

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.651
a BMW parked in a fire lane

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.153
or getting skipped in line
at the deli.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.488
And you do not want to skip
Bernie at the deli.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.056
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
excuse me.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.125
I have number seven.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.860
I've been waiting here
impatiently for 20 minutes

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.862
and you just serve him because
he walks up to the counter

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.996
like he owns the place.

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:52.231
That's wrong, that's crap.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.701
Now I got to go, I got tickets
to Jersey Goys.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.136
Sanders and many other
progressives

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.272
like Congressman Katie Porter
want direct payments

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.540
to Americans and in an interview
last week,

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.776
Porter took issue with the fact
that such payments

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.911
